      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is easier to understand, without such an explanation:\n\n```\nif err !\u003d nil {\n  if os.IsNotExist(err) {\n    // No previous build, nothing to clean.\n    return false, nil\n  } else {\n    return false, err\n  }\n}\nreturn strconv.FormatInt(soongBuildMTime, 10) !\u003d string(mtimeFileContents), nil\n```\n\nPlease don\u0027t rely on variables not being returned in the case of an error occurring. For example,`ReadFile` might return garbage in the first return value if a strange error occurred. This is probably \"fine\" in this practical case, but it\u0027s a dangerous pattern, and it\u0027s harder to understand.",
